      {
        "type": "heading",
        "attrs": {
          "level": 2
        },
        "content": [
          {
            "type": "text",
            "text": "Method"
          }
        ]
      },
      {
        "type": "orderedList",
        "content": [
          {
            "type": "listItem",
            "content": [
              {
                "type": "paragraph",
                "content": [
                  {
                    "type": "text",
                    "text": "Preheat the oven to 180C. Grease and line a 23cm springform tin. Whisk the eggs and sugar together with an electric mixer for 8 to 10 minutes until thick, pale, and tripled in volume. Sift in the flour, cocoa, and baking powder. Fold in gently. Fold in the melted butter. Pour into the tin and bake for 30 to 35 minutes until a skewer comes out clean. Cool completely, then split into three horizontal layers."
                  }
                ]
              }
            ]
          },
          {
            "type": "listItem",
            "content": [
              {
                "type": "paragraph",
                "content": [
                  {
                    "type": "text",
                    "text": "Make the kirsch syrup: simmer the water and sugar until the sugar dissolves. Cool, then stir in 3 tablespoons of kirsch."
                  }
                ]
              }
            ]
          },
          {
            "type": "listItem",
            "content": [
              {
                "type": "paragraph",
                "content": [
                  {
                    "type": "text",
                    "text": "Whip the cream with the icing sugar to stiff peaks. Place the bottom sponge layer on a plate. Brush generously with kirsch syrup. Spread with a thick layer of cream and scatter over half the drained cherries."
                  }
                ]
              }
            ]
          },
          {
            "type": "listItem",
            "content": [
              {
                "type": "paragraph",
                "content": [
                  {
                    "type": "text",
                    "text": "Add the middle sponge layer. Brush with syrup, spread with cream, and add the remaining cherries. Top with the final sponge layer and brush with the remaining syrup."
                  }
                ]
              }
            ]
          },
          {
            "type": "listItem",
            "content": [
              {
                "type": "paragraph",
                "content": [
                  {
                    "type": "text",
                    "text": "Cover the top and sides of the cake with the remaining cream. Press chocolate shavings onto the sides and scatter over the top. Refrigerate for at least 4 hours before serving."
                  }
                ]
              }
            ]
          }
        ]
      },
      {
        "type": "troubleshooter",
        "content": [
          {
            "type": "troubleshooterItem",
            "attrs": {
              "problem": "Sponge is dense rather than light"
            },
            "content": [
              {
                "type": "paragraph",
                "content": [
                  {
                    "type": "text",
                    "text": "The egg and sugar mixture was not whisked for long enough. It should be very thick and pale before you fold in the flour. Also ensure you fold gently with a large spoon to keep the air in."
                  }
                ]
              }
            ]
          },
          {
            "type": "troubleshooterItem",
            "attrs": {
              "problem": "Cream is weeping and sliding"
            },
            "content": [
              {
                "type": "paragraph",
                "content": [
                  {
                    "type": "text",
                    "text": "The cream was not whipped to stiff peaks, or the cake was assembled too warm. Make sure the sponges are completely cold before assembly and the cream is well whipped."
                  }
                ]
              }
            ]
          },
          {
            "type": "troubleshooterItem",
            "attrs": {
              "problem": "Layers slide when slicing"
            },
            "content": [
              {
                "type": "paragraph",
                "content": [
                  {
                    "type": "text",
                    "text": "The cake needs the full chilling time. Do not cut it until it has been refrigerated for at least 4 hours. Use a sharp, thin-bladed knife dipped in hot water."
                  }
                ]
              }
            ]
          }
        ]
      },
      {
        "type": "heading",
        "attrs": {
          "level": 2
        },
        "content": [
          {
            "type": "text",
            "text": "Where this dish lives"
          }
        ]
      },
      {
        "type": "paragraph",
        "content": [
          {
            "type": "text",
            "text": "The Black Forest cake comes from the Schwarzwald region of southwest Germany, where sour cherries and kirsch are both produced. It is the most exported German cake in the world and appears on celebration tables across Europe and beyond. The name is protected in Germany, where the recipe must include kirsch from the region."
          }
        ]
      }
    ]
  }
